course: dictionary
lesson: 13845
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The jingle of keys told me someone was coming.» Here jingle is a light ringing sound, because keys knock together to make it.
explain: «Dad began to jingle the coins in his pocket.» Now jingle is an action: Dad is making the ringing sound. Ask yourself, is this word a thing or something someone is doing? That question helps you choose the meaning.
explain: «The advert's jingle was so catchy that I hummed it all day.» A jingle can also be a short, catchy tune used in an advert on the radio or TV. The words advert and catchy are the clues here, so this meaning fits.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence. The one that still makes sense is the right one.
fact: A jingle can be a light ringing sound made by small metal things, like keys, coins or little bells, knocking together.
fact: To jingle means to make or cause that ringing sound.
fact: A jingle can also be a short, catchy tune used in an advert on the radio or TV.
fact: «A jingle» is a noun, and «to jingle» is a verb: jingles, jingled and jingling are its other forms.
fact: Checking your meaning by putting it into the sentence is a good way to choose between meanings.
exercise: «The jingle of keys told me someone was coming.» What is a jingle here? | A short, catchy advert tune | *A light ringing sound | A loud shout | A kind of key
exercise: «Sleigh bells jingled all the way across the snow.» What does jingled mean? | *Made a light ringing sound | Melted | Shouted loudly | Fell over
exercise: «The radio jingle stuck in my head all morning.» Which meaning of jingle is used? | To run quickly | *A short, catchy tune | A metal key | A cold drink
test: «Dad jingled the coins in his pocket as he walked.» Jingled means? | Lost | Ran | Counted | *Made a ringing sound
test: Ellie said, «The advert's jingle is easy to remember.» Which meaning fits best? | *A short, catchy tune | A tiny insect | A small bell | A loud argument
exam: Which sentence uses jingle as a verb? | The jingle of the keys was loud. | Jingle is a kind of food. | *The bells began to jingle as the sleigh moved. | The jingle on the television was funny.
